				\begin{document}$${{{{{{{\rm{Disc}}}}}}}}({c}_{i})=\frac{{\sum }_{{c}_{j}\in {{{{{{{\rm{Neighbor}}}}}}}}({c}_{i})}\,{{{{{{{\rm{Sim}}}}}}}}\,({c}_{i},{c}_{j})\left| \left(-{\log }_{10}\,{{{{{{{\rm{Activity}}}}}}}}\,({c}_{i})\right)-(-{\log }_{10}{{{{{{{\rm{Activity}}}}}}}}({c}_{j}))\right|}{\Big| \,{{{{{{{\rm{Neighbor}}}}}}}}\,({c}_{i})\Big| },$$\end{document}Disc(ci)=∑cj∈Neighbor(ci)Sim(ci,cj)−log10Activity(ci)−(−log10Activity(cj))Neighbor(ci),where Neighbor(ci) stands for the set of compounds that can form MMPs with ci, and Sim(ci, cj) stands for the Tanimoto similarity between molecular fingerprints of ci and cj. Then, a compound ci was defined as an AC compound if Disc(ci) > 1; Otherwise it was considered a non-AC compound.
